---
import Store from '../layouts/Store.astro';
import ProductArt from '../components/ProductArt.astro';
import products from '../data/products.json';
---
<Store><section class="hero wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM A PLACE. FOR EVERY DAY.</p><h1>Carry a little<br/><em>Odisha.</em></h1><p class="lead">In the words we wear.<br/>In the things we reach for.<br/>In the feeling we take with us.</p><a class="button" href="#collection">Meet the first collection ↗</a><p class="small">T-SHIRT · JHULA BAG · COFFEE CUP · WATER BOTTLE</p></div><div class="hero-art"><ProductArt product={products[0]} large/><div class="hero-tag">01 / THE BLACK UTKAL T-SHIRT<br/><span>One word. A world of belonging.</span></div></div></section>
<div class="ribbon">SEA BLUE. LATERITE EARTH. EVERYDAY BELONGING.</div>
<section class="wrap collection" id="collection"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SMALL FIRST CHAPTER</p><h2>Start with<br/><em>something familiar.</em></h2></div><p>Four everyday objects. One shared identity.<br/>Made to begin a conversation.</p></div><p class="notice">Collection preview: designs, materials, sizes and prices are awaiting vendor samples and approval. You can save a selection on this device; it is not an order.</p><div class="products">{products.map(p=><article><a href={'/product/'+p.id+'/'} class="product-link"><ProductArt product={p}/><div class="product-title"><h3>{p.name}</h3><span>↗</span></div></a><p>{p.collection} · {p.language==='or'?'Odia':'English'}</p><p class="price">Price to be confirmed</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="story" id="story"><div class="wrap story-grid"><p class="eyebrow">THE ODISHA FEELING</p><div><h2>A place you love.<br/><em>A feeling you carry.</em></h2><p>We want everyday objects to open a door: to a word, a place, a memory, a story worth knowing. Our first designs begin with Utkal, in English and in Odia, each in its own space.</p><p>Sea-blue lettering, laterite highlights and warm paper bring the collection together. Flowers and fruits will inform later collections as we listen, research and learn.</p><p class="small">FIRST SUPPLY PLAN: VENDORS IN BANGALORE.<br/>PRODUCT SAMPLES AND PARTNERS ARE STILL TO BE CONFIRMED.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap closing"><p class="eyebrow">A UTKAL COLLECTIVE SUB-PROJECT</p><h2>Start small.<br/><em>Make it worth keeping.</em></h2><p>Utkal Store develops its own products and operations. Its commercial activity remains separate from the editorial decisions of Project Odisha.</p></section></Store>
